// spliced library can meet a sibling at all. src/lib/research-brief.ts
// decides whether there is a record to make: it judges the answer
// member by member against the documents this pass offered, and
// composes an accepted one into the summary and payload pair
// entity_research keeps a result in. src/lib/sanitize-md.ts reduces
// the untrusted text inside it. Neither states the other's rule and
// nothing below states a rule of its own.
//
// THE ORDER IS JUDGE, COMPOSE, REDUCE, and it is not interchangeable.
// research-brief.ts judges and never edits, so a summary spelling the
// data fence is REFUSED rather than cut and an accepted summary is
// composed VERBATIM. Reducing first would hand the judgement an
// edited value and store a row whose text no longer matches what the
// model said, with nothing anywhere recording the difference.
// Reducing last is what keeps the two rules separable.
//
// WHAT IS REDUCED IS THE SUMMARY AND NOT THE PAYLOAD, and the gap is
// the module's own reading rather than an omission here. The
// structured half is carried unread: no contract declares its keys,
// so there is nothing to hold it to, and a walk over an arbitrarily
// nested value is a different module. A hostile string inside fields
// therefore reaches the column as it arrived, and the renderers under
// src/exports/ are where it meets a reduction. The summary is the
// half a person reads as prose, and it is reduced here.
//
// THE OFFERED SET IS CARRIED AND NEVER RE-DERIVED. Prepare Model
// Prompt cut the drained documents down to the ones there was text to
// hand over, and that list travelled through the ledger to get here
// precisely so this node judges the citations against what was
// actually offered. Reading the drain again would be a second
// statement of what was offered, and two statements of that can
// disagree — at which point a citation naming a document the pass
// never handed over is accepted by the disagreement.
